# Dark Matter: Genesis — Core Agent Rules

## Authority stack

1. `.cursor/rules/` (always-applied project rules)
2. `Assets/_Project/GAME_DESIGN_DOCUMENT_5.0.txt` (GDD 5.0)
3. `AGENTS.md`
4. `.cursor/skills/` (additive only — see `skill-precedence.mdc`)

**Disk truth before claiming shipped:** `Assets/_Project/Documentation/Architecture/World_Engine_Disk_Status.md`

## Locked product identity (GDD 5.0)

- **Platforms:** PC primary + consoles (PS5 / Xbox) only. No mobile or WebGL ship target.
- **Economy:** **Aether Credits (AC) only**. No Pi marketplace, wallet, or third-party crypto loops.
- **Setting:** Io 2160 — survival lite RPG, Lite Building base camp, companion-driven expeditions. Player is **Kade**.
- **Roster:** up to 22 base-camp companions; switchable trio of 3 on expeditions.
- **Echoes / thermal / BCP:** Neural Echoes + Aether-9 Resonance Events; single cold/heat meter; Building Control Panels (Overview | Companions | Production | Craft | Changes). Journal Craft = recipe library only.
- **Runtime:** The World Engine (WoOS) on **Unity 6 HDRP** (`6000.4.11f1`). Not URP. Not a ship target for mobile/WebGL.
- **Playable scene:** `Assets/_Project/Scenes/Dark Matter Genesis v1.6.2.unity`

## Live engineering locks (do not contradict)

- **No NavMesh.** Do not add NavMesh baking, `NavMeshSurface` wiring, `NavMeshAgent` gameplay, or deferred NavMesh loads. Terrain tiles must not reference NavMesh assets.
- **Do not retune `Player_v7`** (capsule radius/height, layers, physics). Player layer **8**; Climbable layer **23**. See `dark-matter-genesis-player-physics.mdc`.
- **No NavMesh, motion matching, or a new character controller** for climb. Climb is `DMClimbProfile` + `DMClimbController` on the **Variant**, not a Player_v7 retune.
- **Source control:** git is agent source of truth. Plastic check-in is the user in the Plastic window (no `cm` CLI). Never silent checkout/reset/revert.
- **Editor Auto Refresh is off.** After edits, the user Ctrl+R. Do not `refresh_unity` force/compile unless asked.
- **Do not git-add** untracked L.V.E, mocap packs, `UIElementsSchema`, PlanetPack02, OlegWER, GDKEditionAutoGen.
- **Underground map** is later content. The surface map lower-right `?` / Underground box is the teaser — do not build the second map unless asked.
- **Companion runtime anims** are paused until UITK HUD work is done.
- **All created UI is UITK only.** No new uGUI. See `dark-matter-genesis-uitk-lock.mdc` and `dark-matter-genesis-ui-toolkit.mdc`. Hot Cross uses `Assets/_Project/Art/UI/HotCrossIcons` cutouts only.

## Engineering essentials

- Code under `Assets/_Project/`; reuse existing combat, inventory, quest, save, companion, building, exposure systems.
- **PC first**, then console parity: Input System (KBM + gamepad), scalable UI, solid frame pacing.
- Prefer pooling, events, ScriptableObject config; minimize polling and heavy Update loops.
- **DM / DMI naming** — no new Invector-branded identifiers in `_Project` (see `dm-naming-no-invector.mdc`).
- **UI:** `DarkMatterGenesisUiPalette` / Shift theme (`dark-matter-genesis-ui-palette.mdc`). **All created UI is UITK only** (`dark-matter-genesis-uitk-lock.mdc`).

## Non-negotiable agent workflow

- **No silent restore** — never checkout/reset/revert to older git or depot save points without explicit user confirmation in the current message.
- **No forced Unity refresh** — do not call `refresh_unity` with `mode: force` or `compile: request` unless the user explicitly asks.
- **After script/asset edits:** wait for compile + domain reload to finish, then check Unity console for **errors** before claiming done. See `unity-agent-workflow.mdc`.
- **Before git commit:** Unity console must have no errors; stage scenes, prefabs, materials, terrain, and new assets with script changes. See `unity-agent-workflow.mdc`.
- Do not clone this repo onto an agent VM. Play uses the live Unity folder the editor has open.

